Qwen3.5-4B> Completed analysis of Bischoff et al. 2021 lung adenocarcinoma single-cell RNA-seq data from 3CA (3ca:20764). Investigated whether transcriptional metabolic states form distinct clusters. Key findings: (1) All-gene clustering (k=5) achieves silhouette score 0.694, substantially higher than MP-score-only clustering (k=20, score 0.555), indicating metabolic states do not form the primary organizational structure of the transcriptome. (2) MP scores show distinct distributions across cell types but are weakly correlated with cell complexity (r=0.074). (3) 75.7% of cells are unassigned to metabolic programs. Concluded that while metabolic programs are biologically meaningful, they cannot be used to cluster the single-cell transcriptome independently of other transcriptional features. All required artifacts created: report/main.tex (LaTeX source), report/main.pdf (compiled PDF), results/summary.json (analysis statistics), README.md (documentation). Data verified from 3CA cache with SHA-256 hashes recorded.

